# Delivery & idempotency (transversal)

SoT: `docs/event-delivery-reliability.md` (spec `011`). Applies to **every**
new domain/worker/command — not optional per feature.

## MUST (when the flow writes or publishes)

- Same MySQL transaction: aggregate + audit + outbox (or command outbox)
- Publisher marks published **only after** broker ACK
- Consumers: inbox `UNIQUE (consumer_id, event_id)`
- At-least-once + DLQ + alarm; never silent drop
- Critical HTTP creates: `Idempotency-Key` (`022`) **and** outbox if they emit

## MUST NOT

- `PutEvents` / `SendMessage` inside the HTTP use case (dual-write)
- Skip inbox because “we already have Idempotency-Key”
- Invent a per-domain bus or fire-and-forget side effect
